  "raw": {
    "https://juniata.peopleadmin.com/postings/1841": {
      "title": "Juniata College Applicant Portal",
      "description": "Juniata College Applicant Portal | College Counselor (Part-time, on-site) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help College Counselor (Part-time, on-site) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested candidates are asked to submit the following materials via our on-line application system: Cover-letter, resume and list of references. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Posting Details Position Information Job Title College Counselor (Part-time, on-site) Posting Number 20110674 Pay Rate Starting at $23.74/hr Position Type Part Time/Temporary Position Summary Information Key Responsibilities Juniata College invites applicants for a part-time, on-site college counselor. This position serves as a counselor for students to help a student to address personal, academic, and social stressors. The counselor will provide support through counseling sessions, crisis intervention and planning, outreach, consultation, and prevention services. The counselor makes meaningful contributions to student wellness by providing clinical sound, evidence-based, equitable, and compassionate mental health support. A component of the counselor position includes helping students who have experienced life-altering events and/or trauma; helping students to process their situation and to build resilience. The counselor candidate will have creative capacity to identify needs and build structural outreach to improve the campus experience for students and adhere to the mission of Glaeser Counseling Services: The Glaeser Counseling Services provides mental health services that nurture and promote the dignity, diversity, development, and worth of all individuals. Typical Duties and Responsibilities: • Provide short-term and longer-term mental health counseling or case management appropriate to the level of care at a college counseling center. • Provide therapy using individual, family, couple and/or group modalities. • Collaborate with on-campus partners to develop and implement programs supporting the campus mission of student success. • Assist students in identifying campus resources and making appropriate referrals per request and/or identified need of the student. • Maintain appropriate professional records on each client and communicate client information in a confidential and professional manner. • Provide consultation/training services to faculty, staff, caregivers and students to enhance personal development and wellness. • Develop and implement individualized treatment plan and behavioral goals, consulting with the Director of Counseling and contracted psychiatric team as appropriate. • Inform Director of Counseling of any difficulties related to student client’s satisfaction, treatment issues, procedural concerns, and other departmental or public relations concerns. • Assure that all office procedures, policies, and required reports are developed, followed and completed in accordance with office procedures. • Work with the Director of Counseling to contribute to annual goals and objectives for Glaeser Counseling Services at Juniata College. • Work at designated areas as assigned to provide counseling services; i.e. Glaeser Counseling Services, the SPoT (Safe Place to Talk), Kennedy Sports & Recreation Center, etc. • Perform other related duties as assigned. This position is paid hourly and is not eligible for benefits. Estimated number of hours per week is 20 hours weekly, as arranged. Juniata College is committed to cultivating an equity-minded and equity-engaged campus culture, one that is inclusive and supportive of its students, faculty, and staff. We believe that all members of the College community share the responsibility to value diversity, seek equity, promote a sense of belonging. We seek candidates who are sensitive to the needs of an academic community that is diverse with regard to gender, race, ethnicity, religion, nationality, sexual orientation or identity, disability status, and protected veteran status… EOE Position Qualifications • Master’s degree in clinical counseling, psychology or social work. • Comfortability and/or experiences counseling college age clients. • Licensed Professional Counselor or Licensed Clinical Social Worker preferred. • Ability to work effectively with diverse individuals and groups. • Successful completion of background checks. Supervision Required/Given Operates within established regulations and procedures of Glaeser Counseling Services at Juniata College. Reports directly to the Director of Counseling, and indirectly to the Vice President for Student Life & Dean of Students Preferred Qualifications See position qualifications Physical Demands Special Instructions to Applicants Interested candidates are asked to submit the following materials via our on-line application system: Cover-letter, resume and list of references. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Posting Detail Information Open Date 07/15/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of 3 References Optional Documents Juniata College 1700 Moore Street Huntingdon, PA 16652 Phone: (877) 586-4282 Fax: (814) 641-3199 Email: info@juniata.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://juniata.peopleadmin.com/postings/1580": {
      "title": "Juniata College Applicant Portal",
      "description": "Juniata College Applicant Portal | Shuttle Drivers (Part-Time) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Shuttle Drivers (Part-Time) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Shuttle Drivers (Part-Time) Posting Number 20110431 Pay Rate $10.00/hour Position Type Part Time/Temporary Position Summary Information Key Responsibilities Shuttle Van Drivers are responsible for the safe, timely and professional transportation of employees, visitors, guests and students to and from various locations. Ranging from 15, 12 and 5 passenger vehicles. Responsibilities include: • Able to work well independently with minimal supervision. • Able to work flexible hours, including mornings, evenings and weekends, part-time work. • Greet and welcome passengers in a friendly professional welcoming manner. • Maintain a neat and professional appearance at all times. • Maintain operation of vehicle; fuel vehicle as needed. • Report suspected maintenance issues with vehicle to supervisor at end of shift. • Observe and abide all Federal and State traffic regulations in the respective states in which operating. • Observe all safety laws and ensure passengers adhere to all safety laws. • Assist passengers with placing and securing personal belongings safely in the vehicle. Juniata College is committed to cultivating an equity-minded and equity-engaged campus culture, one that is inclusive and supportive of its students, faculty, and staff. We believe that all members of the College community share the responsibility to value diversity, seek equity, promote a sense of belonging. We seek candidates who are sensitive to the needs of an academic community that is diverse with regard to gender, race, ethnicity, religion, nationality, sexual orientation or identity, disability status, and protected veteran status .…EOE Position Qualifications Drivers must have a valid driver’s license for a minimum of 2 years and a good driving record (no major driving convictions accepted, no minor offenses within 5 years.) Drivers must be at least 21 years of age to apply. Child Abuse and Criminal Background checks and MVR will be completed. Drivers must be flexible as, we run shuttles 7 days per week. This could include daily runs, or monthly shuttles. Drivers are scheduled as needed all hours are on a part-time basis. Successful candidates must complete online safety training and pass a behind the wheel assessment. Supervision Required/Given This position reports to the Transportation Coordinator/ Supervisor. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Detail Information Open Date 07/07/2022 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Walk-In Government Employment Agency Private Employment Agency Employee (please explain in follow up question) Relative (please explain in follow up question) School Advertisement - Source (please explain in follow up question) Other (please explain in follow up question) If you were referred by a person, advertisement or other, please explain here: (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter List of 3 References Juniata College 1700 Moore Street Huntingdon, PA 16652 Phone: (877) 586-4282 Fax: (814) 641-3199 Email: info@juniata.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
