 and implementing training programs for Juniata’s varsity sport programs. Oversee the hiring, training and development of volunteer interns and student employees including handling administrative paperwork and education. Monitor access to fitness center exclusively for Juniata students, faculty, staff and community members. Track liability waiver completion and fitness center usage via software platform system. Collaborate with coaches and Athletic Trainers to monitor strength, fitness and rehabilitation programs. Stay abreast of current advances in physiology and kinesiology of human performance while bringing creative approaches, ideas and solutions to supervisor. Supervise and perform routine daily, weekly, monthly yearly maintenance of equipment. Work with Athletic Operations staff to put in work orders for facility maintenance as needed. Create and maintain positive relationships with campus partners Juniata College is committed to cultivating an equity-minded and equity-engaged campus culture, one that is inclusive and supportive of its students, faculty, and staff. We believe that all members of the College community share the responsibility to value diversity, seek equity, promote a sense of belonging. We seek candidates who are sensitive to the needs of an academic community that is diverse with regard to gender, race, ethnicity, religion, nationality, sexual orientation or identity, disability status, and protected veteran status… AA/ EOE Position Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree required Certified in CPR , First Aid, AED is required. Certification from NSCA - CSCS or CSCCa- SCCC required. Knowledge and adherence to Juniata College, NCAA Division III and Conference (Landmark and CVC ) rules and regulations Valid driver’s license required, clear of major violations. Juniata College reserves the right to review driving records to determine suitability for position. Experience at Collegiate level preferred Supervision Required/Given This position reports to the Assistant Athletic Director for Sport Performance. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Special Instructions to Applicants It is Juniata College’s policy to conduct background checks. Valid driver’s license required, clear of major violations. Juniata College reserves the right to review driving records to determine suitability for position. Posting Detail Information Open Date 05/20/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled No Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of 3 References Optional Documents Juniata College 1700 Moore Street Huntingdon, PA 16652 Phone: (877) 586-4282 Fax: (814) 641-3199 Email: info@juniata.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
