    "https://juniata.peopleadmin.com/postings/1819": {
      "title": "Juniata College Applicant Portal | Lecturer in Business",
      "description": "Juniata College Applicant Portal | Lecturer in Business Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lecturer in Business Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants should submit 1) a cover letter describing qualifications and teaching interests, 2) curriculum vitae or resume, 3) contact information for three professional references, and 4) unofficial graduate transcripts (official transcripts required upon hire) through the online portal. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position(s) is filled. Juniata College conducts background checks. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Lecturer in Business Posting Number 20110669 Pay Rate Fixed rate per credit hour Position Type Part Time/Temporary Position Summary Information Key Responsibilities Juniata College invites applications for part-time adjunct faculty to teach one or more of the following courses beginning in the Fall 2026 semester: · Business Law (undergraduate, in-person) · Financial Management I (undergraduate, in-person) · Production and Operations Management (graduate, online **Applicants must reside in Pennsylvania or an approved U.S. state where the college is authorized to employ remote staff. We are unable to consider candidates located outside of these areas or outside the United States. ) Applicants are encouraged to indicate which course(s) they are qualified and interested in teaching. The undergraduate courses are taught on Juniata’s campus in Huntingdon, Pennsylvania. A hybrid option would be considered if necessary. The graduate course is delivered online through the College’s graduate programs. Juniata College is a nationally recognized liberal arts college committed to academic excellence, engaged learning, and close faculty-student interaction. We seek an instructor who combines disciplinary expertise with a commitment to student success and high-quality teaching. Primary Responsibilities Teach Business Law or Financial Management I in a face-to-face classroom setting. Teach Production and Operations Management in an online graduate format. Prepare course materials, syllabi, assignments, and assessments consistent with departmental learning outcomes. Maintain regular communication with students and provide timely feedback on assignments. Submit final grades and fulfill other instructional responsibilities in accordance with College policies. Work collaboratively with department faculty to ensure course quality and consistency. Juniata College is committed to cultivating an equity-minded and equity-engaged campus culture, one that is inclusive and supportive of its students, faculty, and staff. We believe that all members of the College community share the responsibility to value diversity, seek equity, promote a sense of belonging. We seek candidates who are sensitive to the needs of an academic community that is diverse with regard to gender, race, ethnicity, religion, nationality, sexual orientation or identity, disability status, and protected veteran status ..…EOE Position Qualifications Master’s degree in Business Administration, Finance, Management, or a closely related discipline from an accredited institution. Demonstrated ability to teach business courses effectively at the undergraduate and/or graduate level. Strong written and interpersonal communication skills. Supervision Required/Given This position reports to the Accounting, Business, and Economics Department Chair. Preferred Qualifications Doctorate (Ph.D., DBA , JD, or other appropriate terminal degree) in a related field. Professional experience in business, finance, operations, or law. Prior college teaching experience in both traditional classroom and online environments. Experience using a learning management system (e.g., Moodle, Canvas, Blackboard). Physical Demands Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants should submit 1) a cover letter describing qualifications and teaching interests, 2) curriculum vitae or resume, 3) contact information for three professional references, and 4) unofficial graduate transcripts (official transcripts required upon hire) through the online portal. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position(s) is filled. Juniata College conducts background checks. Posting Detail Information Open Date 06/29/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Transcripts Optional Documents Resume Curriculum Vitae List of 3 References Juniata College 1700 Moore Street Huntingdon, PA 16652 Phone: (877) 586-4282 Fax: (814) 641-3199 Email: info@juniata.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://juniata.peopleadmin.com/postings/1825": {
      "title": "Juniata College Applicant Portal | Lecturer in Statistics",
      "description": "Juniata College Applicant Portal | Lecturer in Statistics Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lecturer in Statistics Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants should submit 1) a cover letter describing qualifications and teaching interests, 2) curriculum vitae or resume, 3) contact information for three professional references through the online portal. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position(s) is filled. Juniata College conducts background checks. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Lecturer in Statistics Posting Number 20110672 Pay Rate Fixed rate per credit hour Position Type Part Time/Temporary Position Summary Information Key Responsibilities Juniata College invites applications for part-time adjunct faculty to teach one or more courses in statistics or quantitative methods for business beginning in the Fall 2026 semester. Courses are at that undergraduate level. Applicants are encouraged to indicate which course(s) they are qualified and interested in teaching. The undergraduate courses are taught on Juniata’s campus in Huntingdon, Pennsylvania. Juniata College is a nationally recognized liberal arts college committed to academic excellence, engaged learning, and close faculty-student interaction. We seek an instructor who combines disciplinary expertise with a commitment to student success and high-quality teaching. Primary Responsibilities Teach in a face-to-face classroom setting. Prepare course materials, syllabi, assignments, and assessments consistent with departmental learning outcomes. Maintain regular communication with students and provide timely feedback on assignments. Submit final grades and fulfill other instructional responsibilities in accordance with College policies. Work collaboratively with department faculty to ensure course quality and consistency. Juniata College is committed to cultivating an equity-minded and equity-engaged campus culture, one that is inclusive and supportive of its students, faculty, and staff. We believe that all members of the College community share the responsibility to value diversity, seek equity, promote a sense of belonging. We seek candidates who are sensitive to the needs of an academic community that is diverse with regard to gender, race, ethnicity, religion, nationality, sexual orientation or identity, disability status, and protected veteran status ..…EOE Position Qualifications Master’s degree in Business Administration, Finance, Management, or a closely related discipline from an accredited institution. Demonstrated ability to teach business courses effectively at the undergraduate and/or graduate level. Strong written and interpersonal communication skills. Supervision Required/Given This position reports to the Accounting, Business, and Economics Department Chair. Preferred Qualifications Doctorate (Ph.D., DBA , JD, or other appropriate terminal degree) in a related field. Professional experience in business. Prior college teaching experience in both traditional classroom. Experience using a learning management system (e.g., Moodle, Canvas, Blackboard). Physical Demands Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants should submit 1) a cover letter describing qualifications and teaching interests, 2) curriculum vitae or resume, 3) contact information for three professional references through the online portal. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position(s) is filled. Juniata College conducts background checks. Posting Detail Information Open Date 07/10/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Optional Documents Resume Transcripts Curriculum Vitae List of 3 References Juniata College 1700 Moore Street Huntingdon, PA 16652 Phone: (877) 586-4282 Fax: (814) 641-3199 Email: info@juniata.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
